! Resting cavity under a SLOPING ice shelf — the Phase-5 physics gate and
! the Phase-6 baseline.
!
! WHAT THIS IS.  A stratified ice-shelf cavity, initialised at rest, with
! nothing that can move it: flat bed, no wind, no surface flux, no bottom
! drag, no vertical mixing closure, NO lateral viscosity, no melt.  The ice
! base slopes linearly from the grounding line to a calving front, beyond
! which the domain is open ocean.  The only thing left that can generate a
! velocity is the PRESSURE-GRADIENT DISCRETISATION, which is exactly what
! the case is here to measure.
!
! The load partition under test (`&ocean_cavity_dyn_nml` + `p_top_in_bc`):
!
!     bt_H_ref  = b - z_draft                   the barotropic DATUM
!     p_ice_ref = rho_ref*GRAVITY*z_draft       the Boussinesq-isostatic load
!     ms%p_top  = p_ice_ref + sf%p_surf         the PGF/EOS surface BC
!     pa(nz+1)  = rho_ref*g*eta_geo + p_top     -> rho_ref*g*eta_trim at rest
!
! THE BALANCED INITIAL STATE (`trim_ic_for_p_surf`, MOM6
! TRIM_IC_FOR_P_SURF / `trim_for_ice`).  `p_ice_ref` is the displaced
! weight at the REFERENCE density; the stratified water it displaces
! weighs g*int_{-z_draft}^{0} rho dz, lighter by g*I(z_draft),
! I = int (rho - rho_ref) dz = -0.2878*z_d + 4.197e-4*z_d^2 kg/m2 here
! (surface water is 0.29 kg/m3 lighter than rho_ref, N^2 = 8.0e-6).  At
! eta = 0 every level under the ice would then sit -g*I off the open
! ocean at the same z: a DEPTH-UNIFORM force
! (g/rho_ref)*(rho(-z_draft) - rho_ref)*grad(z_draft), up to 1.8e-5 m/s^2
! (-8.4e-6 at the grounding end, +1.8e-5 near the front, zero at
! z_draft = 343 m), ~5000x the truncation this case measures.  The legacy
! split discarded it with the depth mean; the MOM6 split
! (`&ocean_bt_nml bc_pgf_forcing`, default) hands it to the barotropic
! mode, which adjusted to it on day 1 (En 1.06E-06, over the bar).  As in
! MOM6, the LOAD is kept (the ice mass is what is prescribed) and the
! initial column top moves to the depth s where the water above weighs
! the load, g*int_{-s}^{0} rho dz = p_ice_ref: eta_trim = z_draft - s,
! -3.0 mm at the front to -4.80 cm at z_draft = 343 m, with T/S
! evaluated at the trimmed layer centres.  The interface pressures are
! then the open ocean's exactly; what the depth mean still carries is
! truncation (measured at the PGF on this geometry, 1.6e-5 -> 3.9e-8
! m/s^2: `test_ocean_cavity_load::trim_ic_balances_the_depth_mean_pfu`).
! So the barotropic mode starts balanced and the residual is the FV-MOM6
! truncation error alone.
!
! WHY THE INITIAL CONDITION USES `&ocean_zinit_nml source = "linear"`.
! Under `VCOORD_SIGMA` the layer interfaces TILT with the ice base.  The
! `&tracer_nml T_init_surface` / `S_init_*` family lays a profile out
! linearly in LAYER INDEX, i.e. along the tilted coordinate — which tilts
! the isopycnals with the lid and is NOT a state of rest, so the run would
! measure a real baroclinic adjustment rather than a numerical error.  The
! zinit "linear" source evaluates T(z)/S(z) at each layer centre's TRUE
! GEOPOTENTIAL depth (column top at `z = -z_draft + eta_trim`), so the
! isopycnals are flat in z on every column, sloping lid included.
!
! GEOMETRY (2-D in x; the y direction is 6 cells of the same column).
!   * 48 x 6 x 15 @ dx = dy = 2 km  ->  96 km x 12 km, flat bed at 720 m.
!   * Ice base: z_draft = 570 - 6.9e-3*(x + 10 km), so 494 m at the first
!     interior column and 11 m at the last shelf column; the shelf box ends
!     at x = 72 km (the CALVING FRONT) and the remaining 24 km is open
!     ocean (z_draft = 0).  The anchor x0 = -10 km puts the ghost columns
!     INSIDE the box so they carry the analytic continuation of the draft
!     rather than a step to zero at the wall.
!   * Per-face draft step: 13.8 m in the shelf interior, 11.1 m at the
!     calving front — the front is deliberately NOT the biggest step in the
!     domain.  The residual is CUBIC in that step (below), so a 100 m
!     ISOMIP+-style calving cliff would dominate the run and the case would
!     stop measuring the sloping lid.  That regime is real and belongs to
!     the correction work: Yung et al. (2026) §3.4.2 record that MOM6-LAYER
!     suppresses its calving criterion near the ice front "to minimise
!     pressure gradient errors", and MPAS-Ocean caps the coordinate's Haney
!     number at 5 for the same reason.  This file is not the place to hide
!     it, and not the place to be dominated by it either.
!   * Water column 226 m at the grounding end, 709 m at the front — every
!     column far above `h_min_cavity = 40 m` (MOM6-LAYER's ISOMIP+ minimum,
!     Yung et al. 2026 §3.4.2), so nothing is grounded and, under sigma, no
!     layer can vanish.  Configure reports 0 of 288 columns grounded.
!
! STRATIFICATION — ISOMIP+ COLD, as printed (Asay-Davis et al. 2016,
! Eq. 23 + Tables 4-5), converted to roundabout's DIMENSIONAL linear EOS:
!   T = -1.9 degC everywhere (T0 = T_bot);  S = 33.8 -> 34.55 over 720 m.
!   alpha_lin = 3.733e-5 /degC, beta_lin = 7.843e-4 /PSU, rho_ref = 1027.51
!     =>  alpha_T = rho_0*alpha_lin = 3.8356948e-2 kg/m3/degC
!         beta_S  = rho_0*beta_lin  = 8.0587609e-1 kg/m3/PSU
!   (feeding the FRACTIONAL coefficients straight in under-states the
!   density response ~1000x and looks like a plausible weak run).
!   N^2 = -(g/rho_0)*beta_S*dS/dz = 8.01e-6 s^-2.
!   f-plane at 75 S: f = -2*Omega*sin(75 deg) = -1.409e-4 s^-1.
!
! WHAT TO EXPECT, derived.  Flat bed + sigma makes the interface gap
! between two columns `De(K) = sigma_K*D`, with `D` the draft step across
! the face, and the FV-MOM6 Pass-3 numerator telescopes into a trapezoid
! error `G(K) = -(De(K)^3/12)*rho_0*N^2`.  Its deviation from the depth
! mean (what the legacy split, which replaced the depth mean, left) is
!
!     PFu(k) - <PFu>_h = N^2 * D^3 * (3*sigma_k^2 - 1) / (12*dx*Hbar)
!
! — SECOND order in dx, CUBIC in the draft slope, independent of nz,
! peaking at the ice base (sigma = 1) at `a_peak = N^2*D^3/(6*dx*Hbar)`.
! With N^2 = 8.01e-6, D = 13.8 m, dx = 2000 m, Hbar = 470 m:
!
!     a_peak = 3.73e-9 m/s^2
!     geostrophic scale U = a_peak/|f| = 2.65e-5 m/s  ->  En ~ 3.5e-10
!
! Under the MOM6 split the depth MEAN reaches the barotropic mode too, and
! it carries one more truncation term the deviation above does not: the
! Pass-3 in-layer integral treats each layer's density as uniform (short
! by g*rho_z*h^3/12), and sigma layers h = W/nz differ across a face, so
! the depth mean carries a DEPTH-UNIFORM ~N^2*W*dW/(4*nz^2*dx) = 1-4e-8
! m/s^2 (measured at the PGF, see above).  Curl-free in this 2-D geometry,
! it is balanced by a sub-millimetre surface tilt; its seiche is
! |u| ~ a*L/(2c) ~ 2e-5 m/s, inside the plateau below.
!
! MEASURED, gfortran 15.1 Release, single rank, 2026-09-25, with the
! trimmed IC and the default MOM6 split.  En is the domain-mean specific
! KE from the daily [stats] line.
!
!   pred_corr (the DEFAULT, and the base case):
!     day  1   1.117E-09      day 22   2.495E-09      day 40   6.434E-07
!     day  5   1.381E-09      day 25   3.875E-09      day 50   2.523E-06
!     day 10   1.877E-09      day 30   2.298E-08      day 60   3.492E-06
!     day 20   1.645E-09      day 35   1.552E-07
!
!   ssp_rk2 (the automatic __ssp_rk2 twin):
!     day 10   1.875E-09      day 15   5.757E-06      day 30   1.850E-04
!     day 11   1.577E-09      day 20   4.237E-05
!
!   Controls on the same tree (pred_corr):
!     * UNtrimmed (trim_ic_for_p_surf = .false.): the barotropic mode
!       adjusts to the load shortfall on day 1 and the late mode grows
!       from that larger seed -- 1.061E-06 (d1, over the REST_1MM_S bar),
!       2.108E-07 (d5), 1.020E-08 (d10), 4.371E-09 (d20), 1.316E-07 (d30).
!     * the legacy split (`&ocean_bt_nml bc_pgf_forcing = .false.`, no
!       trim), which discards the depth mean and so both the shortfall and
!       the in-layer term: 1.030E-09 (d1), 1.346E-09 (d5), 1.626E-09
!       (d10), 2.070E-09 (d20), 5.275E-09 (d25), 3.043E-08 (d30),
!       3.894E-06 (d60) -- the table this file carried through 2026-09-24,
!       and within 30 % of the trimmed default at every sample.  (ssp_rk2,
!       legacy: 1.981E-09 d11, 4.617E-06 d15, 1.652E-04 d30.)
!
! Cross-toolchain (legacy split, 2026-09-20): the GPU build (nvfortran
! 26.5, -stdpar=gpu, cc70, one Tesla V100-DGXS, 4320 steps in 74.6 s) read
! 3.043E-08 at day 30 — every printed digit of the gfortran answer, on a
! different compiler and a different execution model.  The measurement is
! the algorithm, not an FMA accident.
!
! READ IT IN TWO PARTS.
!
! (a) THE PLATEAU, days 1-20, is the measurement.  En sits at 0.9-1.9E-09,
!     i.e. |u|_rms = 4.2-6.2e-05 m/s, against the derived 3.5E-10 / 2.6e-05
!     m/s.  Two to three times a peak-acceleration estimate compared against
!     a domain rms is as close as that formula can be asked to come, and it
!     is the number the sloping-surface PGF corrections have to beat.  Two
!     controls pin it down: with a FLAT lid (`cavity_flat_lid_rest.nml`,
!     every De(K) = 0) En is EXACTLY 0.000E+00 for 30 days, and with the
!     stratification removed (`cavity_uniform_rho_rest.nml`, every G(K) = 0)
!     it is 1.34E-20.  The residual is the `rho_0*N^2*De^3` term and nothing
!     else.
!
! (b) THE GROWTH, from day ~22, is the FINDING, and it is why this file is
!     a Phase-6 baseline rather than a passing gate.  En leaves the plateau
!     on a ~3.2-day e-folding, then SATURATES: 3.5E-06 by day 60 (2.6 mm/s
!     rms) with the rate clearly decaying, every budget residual still at
!     8e-13 relative, no CFL truncation and no velocity clamping.  It is
!     bounded, not runaway.  Characterised by substitution (under the
!     legacy split, 2026-09-20, whose curve the trimmed default tracks):
!       * dt 600 -> 300 reproduces the curve (day 30: 3.069E-08 vs
!         3.043E-08).  It is NOT an (omega*dt)^n outer-split mode.
!       * ISOMIP+'s own Laplacian (Table 4, nu_h = 6.0 m2/s) only DELAYS it
!         ~10 days: peak 1.13E-09 at day 2, minimum 9.6E-11 at day 20,
!         9.65E-10 at day 30, 1.24E-06 at day 60.
!       * a scale-selective biharmonic (nu_4 = 1.0e7, the dx^4-scaled
!         equivalent of `resting_stratified_channel`'s 5e8 at 5 km) also
!         only delays it: 3.58E-10 at day 30, 6.69E-07 at day 60.  So the
!         mode is not purely grid-scale and no defensible dissipation
!         removes it.
!       * flat lid and uniform density are both bit-zero, so the mode is
!         entirely downstream of the sloping-lid PGF error: remove the
!         source and it does not exist.
!     ssp_rk2 then amplifies the same wave field catastrophically from day
!     12 (1.85E-04 at day 30, 8000x the default) — which is what
!     EXPERIMENTAL on that scheme means, stated as a number, exactly as in
!     `validation_examples/ocean/eady/resting_stratified_channel.nml`.
!
! THE GATE.  `tests/regression/stability_manifest.py` runs this at
! `en_rest_max = REST_1MM_S` (0.5e-06 m2/s2, 1 mm/s), the bar the sloped
! resting family already uses and the velocity a resting sub-shelf cavity
! has no excuse to exceed; the measured day-30 peak of 2.298E-08 clears it
! by 22x in energy, 4.7x in velocity.  At tier 1 (30 days) it is carried
! as a SCOPED XFAIL on `energy:rest-settles` only, because (b) means the
! final sample is the peak at every horizon past day ~22 and short of
! saturation; the 20-day tier-2 twin ends on the plateau (final 1.645E-09
! = 88 % of its 1.877E-09 day-10 peak) and settles.  It does NOT clear the
! tighter `REST_100UM_S` (0.5e-08) the Phase-5 design proposed — day 30 is
! 4.6x over it — and that is recorded here deliberately rather than
! legislated away:
! restoring it is the Phase-6 acceptance criterion.  Do not close either by
! widening the bar, by shortening the run, or by putting viscosity into
! this file.
!
! AGAINST THE LITERATURE.  Yung, Hallberg, Adcroft & Morrison (2026),
! "Assessment of a Finite Volume Discretization of the Horizontal Pressure
! Gradient Force Beneath Sloping Ice Shelves", JAMES 18, e2025MS005645,
! doi:10.1029/2025MS005645, is the paper that fixes this class of error.
! Their abstract: "spurious velocities reduced to order 10^-9 m s^-1 or
! smaller in quiet, linear stratification test cases"; their sigma-
! coordinate icemount goes "from order 10^-7 m s^-1 in the linear surface
! pressure construction (Figure 7c) to 10^-12 m s^-1 (Figure 7d)" (§5.1.2),
! and their 2-D idealised ice shelf "from order 10^-2 m s^-1 (not shown) to
! ... order 10^-9 m s^-1 or less" (§5.2).  This build implements NONE of
! their three corrections (nonlinear surface pressure reconstruction §3.1,
! interior reference interface §3.2, MWIPG §3.3.2), so at their own 10-day
! horizon it sits at |u|_rms = 6.1e-05 m/s.  Read that comparison with the
! two configuration differences in front of you: their runs carry a
! Laplacian viscosity (1000 m2/s for the icemount) plus top and bottom drag
! (c_D = 0.002, U_bg = 0.05 m/s, ~1-day spin-down), and this file carries
! NO dissipation at all by design, so it integrates the spurious force
! instead of arresting it.  With ISOMIP+'s nu_h = 6.0 m2/s this file read
! 3.73E-10 (|u|_rms = 2.7e-05 m/s) at day 10 (legacy split) — still above their
! uncorrected sigma figure.  The gap is the work, not the measurement.
!
! Run:
!   ./build/rdb validation_examples/ocean/ice_shelf_cavity/cavity_sloping_lid_rest.nml
!
! NOTE the configure-time WARNING about `&ocean_psurf_nml in_eos`: the
! in-situ EOS ignores the 5.26 MPa ice load.  With the LINEAR equation of
! state selected here there is no pressure dependence at all, so the load
! in the EOS is literally inert and the warning is informational.  It
! matters for the nonlinear/ISOMIP+ thermodynamic cases, not for this one.

&sim_nml
   sim_type = "ocean"
/

&grid_nml
   nx     = 48
   ny     = 6
   dx     = 2000.0
   dy     = 2000.0
   nghost = 2
/

&time_nml
   t_end        = 2592000.0   ! 30 days
   dt_fixed     = 600.0       ! 10 min outer
   cfl_interval = 1
/

&physics_nml
   coriolis_f    = -1.409e-4   ! f-plane at 75 S (ISOMIP+ 3.1.1)
   wind_stress_x = 0.0
   wind_stress_y = 0.0
/

&nonhydrostatic_nml
   nz_layers = 15
/

&vcoord_nml
   vcoord_type = "sigma"       ! terrain-following: follows the ice base
/

&ocean_topo_nml
   topo_config    = "flat"
   max_depth      = 720.0      ! ISOMIP+ z_b,deep
   wind_config    = "constant"
   taux_magnitude = 0.0
   coriolis_beta  = 0.0
   coriolis_y_ref = 0.0
/

&ocean_cavity_dyn_nml
   enable       = .true.
   draft_config = "linear"
   draft_depth  = 570.0        ! draft AT draft_x0
   draft_slope  = -6.9e-3      ! shallows toward the calving front
   draft_x0     = -10000.0     ! anchor OUTSIDE the domain so ghosts are iced
   draft_x1     = 72000.0      ! the CALVING FRONT; open ocean beyond
   h_min_cavity = 40.0         ! MOM6-LAYER's ISOMIP+ minimum column
   trim_ic_for_p_surf = .true. ! MOM6 TRIM_IC_FOR_P_SURF: start the column
                               ! top where the stratified water above it
                               ! weighs the load (header) -- a real rest
/

&ocean_pgf_nml
   form          = "fv_mom6"   ! the only form with an injectable top BC
   p_top_in_bc   = .true.      ! REQUIRED for a varying draft
   maxvel        = 2.0
/

&ocean_eos_nml
   eos = "linear"
/

&ocean_ic_nml
   alpha_T = 3.8356948e-2      ! rho_0 * 3.733e-5 /degC   (ISOMIP+)
   beta_S  = 8.0587609e-1      ! rho_0 * 7.843e-4 /PSU    (ISOMIP+)
   T_ref   = -1.0              ! ISOMIP+ Table 4
   S_ref   = 34.2
   rho_0   = 1027.51
/

&ocean_zinit_nml
   enable    = .true.
   source    = "linear"        ! analytic T(z)/S(z) at the TRUE geopotential
                               ! depth -- flat isopycnals under a tilted lid
   lin_t_ref = -1.9            ! ISOMIP+ COLD: T0 = T_bot, no thermal gradient
   lin_dt_dz = 0.0
   lin_s_ref = 33.8            ! S at z = 0
   lin_ds_dz = -1.0416667e-3   ! (33.8 - 34.55)/720, z positive UP
/

&tracer_nml
   ! Overwritten by the zinit overlay on the interior AND the ghosts; kept
   ! consistent so a reader is not misled about the state being seeded.
   initial_temperature = -1.9
   initial_salinity    = 34.175
/

&ocean_coriolis_nml
   form = "sadourny"
/

&ocean_hvisc_nml
   ! Zero, deliberately: viscosity damps the spurious flow's LEVEL without
   ! removing what produces it (measured above: nu_h = 6 and nu_4 = 1e7 each
   ! delay the growth ~10 days and change nothing else), so leaving any in
   ! would let a PGF regression hide behind it.  There is no real flow here
   ! to control.
   nu_h = 0.0
   nu_4 = 0.0
/

&ocean_bdrag_nml
   ! No drag: the measurement must not be flattered by dissipation.
   form = "quadratic"
   cd   = 0.0
/

&ocean_vmix_nml
   use_closure = .false.       ! pure dyn-core: no mixing anywhere
   use_kpp     = .false.
/

&ocean_bt_nml
   ! split_scheme is DELIBERATELY not pinned: the default (pred_corr) is the
   ! base case and the stability suite builds the __ssp_rk2 twin from the
   ! same file.  Pinning either would delete that comparison.
   auto_n_inner = .true.
/

&ocean_diag_nml
   enabled  = .true.
   filename = "cavity_sloping_lid_rest"
   dt_out   = 86400.0          ! daily
/

&output_nml
   output_dir     = "./out_cavity_sloping_lid_rest"
   output_to_file = .false.
/

&logging_nml
   log_level       = "info"
   status_interval = 86400.0
/
